<region region-id="4" left="18.00" top="124.00" width="572.00" height="30.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="134.00" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Normal" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">Codes: AASHTO LRFD Bridge Design Specifications, 10th edition (2024); FDOT Structures Design Guidelines, January 2026, 4.1.4A–C; inherited C005 sectional relations.</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="5" left="18.00" top="160.00" width="572.00" height="30.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="170.00" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Normal" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">Tool status: CHECK FAILURES — revise the trial cage or section. Inputs are highlighted yellow; key results are boxed.</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="6" left="18.00" top="206.00" width="572.00" height="22.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="221.00" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Heading 1" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">1. Scope</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="7" left="18.00" top="234.00" width="572.00" height="121.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="244.00" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="List" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">• Computed here: sectional flexure, minimum steel, strain and Service I crack control in regions N (top steel), P (bottom steel at the piles) and B (bottom steel with the added span bars); the shear depth; actual-cage shear, longitudinal tension, torsion screen and minimum transverse steel at the governing stations found by the tool&#x27;s station search; the governing transverse spacing; face shrinkage and temperature steel; skin steel; and the governing hook development.</p><p style="List" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">• Taken from the tool and not recomputed: the station search itself, the intersected-leg window areas and the developed (credited) steel areas (shown as inputs), the detailing and geometry flags, transverse anchorage, the end grid and the D-regions.</p><p style="List" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">• Service III (D-007) and fatigue remain pending.</p></text>
</region>
